  "worked_solution": "If the maple population is $P,$ then the rate of change of the population is $\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t},$ where $t$ is the time in years.\n\nSince $75$ new maple trees are added every year, the rate of change of the population of the maples is given by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t}=75.\n$$",
